		<item>
		<title>Operation Overload: how pro-Russian actors flood newsrooms with fake content and seek to divert their efforts</title>
		<link>https://checkfirst.network/operation-overload-how-pro-russian-actors-flood-newsrooms-with-fake-content-and-seek-to-divert-their-efforts/</link>
		<pubDate>Tue, 04 Jun 2024 03:55:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Publications]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://checkfirst.network/?p=2472</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>“Please Check”. More than 800 organisations, among which many media outlets have been flooded with emails and social media mentions urging them to verify dubious claims undermining Ukraine, France and Germany for the most part. The issue is that these solicitations are part of a massive pro-Russian operation, still ongoing at the time of writing.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://checkfirst.network/operation-overload-how-pro-russian-actors-flood-newsrooms-with-fake-content-and-seek-to-divert-their-efforts/">Operation Overload: how pro-Russian actors flood newsrooms with fake content and seek to divert their efforts</a> appeared first on <a href="https://checkfirst.network">CheckFirst</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
		
		
